  "details": "Mirrors and Custom avatars can cause massive Lag. Any mirrors in the game cause FPS drops of up too 20fps when alone and of there are other players with custom avatars (i.e in VOID CLUB) \n\nthe game runs sub 30 FPS or lower even on \"VR LOW\" and when I already have the game at 90% render on Steam VR\n\nKind of tired of getting sick sitting infront of a mirror at 10 -> 30 FPS infront of a mirror with less then 10 people sitting in front of it\n\nthere is also LAG at distance and Mirrors do not shut off even when you leave the world and come back so when you come back into the world it loads the mirror and sometimes the game will crash. \n\nwhen more then 5 people are in the same world the game Struggles too even RUN when you are alone in the box you get 90FPS locked. when more than 3 people - 5 people the game auto locks too 60 then any more than 5 it wont go any higher than 30FPS.\n\n\n\nOptimize the game please. been playing for 2 years now and the game is still having a hard time even running. \n\n\n\nits really funny that I can play NO MANS SKY VR and get over 100FPS on High VR settings and 110% render and it runs better when objectively No mans sky is less optimized.  Please pay attention too your canny. \n\n\n\n\nSuggestion:\nMulticore/ make the game able too run on Multiple cores (since VRCHAT is CPU HEAVY)\n\n\nNow I can understand that just \"updating unity\" is hard for the team because it breaks SDK however Updating too unity 2019 would S U B S T A N T I A L L Y make this game run better, it takes time too do this since all the files have too be transferd from 2017 Unity LT but this would bring back people who cant play the game at all due too the performance issues\n\nnow to be honest There really needs too be a \n\"VR RECOMMENDED and MINIMAL SPEC on steam for this\"\n\n\n\n\nMy system\nRyzen 7 1800X (OC 4.0Ghz) /8-CORE PROCESSOR \n\nGTX 1070 TI Strix 8GB (OC 1900Mhz / 8014 Mhz Memory boost)\n\n32GB 3200Mhz Ram\n\nVrchat is on 150GB SSD",
